<article class="env-definition" id="02ZI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02ZI">Definition <span data-tag="02ZI">8.5.1</span>.</a> A <em>stack in groupoids</em> over a site $\mathcal{C}$ is a category $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ over $\mathcal{C}$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ is fibred in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$ (see Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/003T" data-tag="003T">4.35.1</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$, for all $x, y\in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{S}_ U)$ the presheaf $\mathit{Isom}(x, y)$ is a sheaf on the site $\mathcal{C}/U$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all coverings $\mathcal{U} = \{ U_ i \to U\} $ in $\mathcal{C}$, all descent data $(x_ i, \phi _{ij})$ for $\mathcal{U}$ are effective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>